DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260924T000402Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20180803T190000Z
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20180803T200000Z
UID:calendar-event-1660457604@schoology.com
URL;VALUE=URI:http://schoology.tesd.net/event/1660457604/profile
SUMMARY:Student schedules will be available to view in Home Access Center
DESCRIPTION: Welcome to the 2018-19 school year at Conestoga! Student schedules will be  \navailable to view in Home Access Center on August 3at 3:00pm. Home Access  \nCenter (HAC) can be accessed at the following web address:  \n*https://hac.tesd.net/ [1]* Please review the schedule carefully to be  \ncertain it is accurate.  Students will receive their lunch assignment  \nduring homeroom on the first day of school. If you experience difficulty  \naccessing your child’s schedule in HAC\, please email  \nfamilyhelpdesk@tesd.net [2]\n\n\n[1] https://hac.tesd.net/\n[2] mailto:familyhelpdesk@tesd.net - Link: http://schoology.tesd.net/event/1660457604/profile
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260924T000402Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20180820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20180825
UID:calendar-event-1662913524@schoology.com
URL;VALUE=URI:http://schoology.tesd.net/event/1662913524/profile
SUMMARY:Senior Parking Application
DESCRIPTION:* *\n\n*Senior Parking Permit Applications for Eligible Seniors will be accepted  \nstarting*\n\n* *\n\n*/Monday\, August 20\, 2018/** in Room 208 /from 8:00AM-12:00PM and  \n1:00PM-2:30PM/*. *Parking Permits will not be issued until Monday\, August 20\,  \n2018.*\n\n* \nAll students must present the following information when applying for a  \npermit:*\n\n \n\n1)       Current PA Vehicle Registration Card for vehicle *(Copy)*\n\n2)       Valid Driver's License *(Copy)*\n\n3)       Pennsylvania Insurance Identification Card *(Copy)*\n\n4)       Student ID\, schedule\, etc. to verify grade level\n\n5)       Processing fee of *$180.00-Please make checks payable to CHS*\n\n6)       Completed Parking Registration form with parent and student  \nsignatures signed in the presence of a school official or notarized\n\n7)       Completed Medical Emergency Card (green) or proof of  \nsubmission to the Nurse\n\n8)       Completed Diploma Card\, Authorization for Transcript Release  \nForm or proof of submission to Guidance\n\n9)       Evidence that all debts and obligations have been satisfied.  \nDirect debt questions to the Business Office\, Room 116\n\n10)      Completed Extended Experience Application (if applicable)\n\n11)      Student 2018-2019 Academic Schedule\n\n12)      Updated / Required Immunization Records - Link: http://schoology.tesd.net/event/1662913524/profile
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260924T000402Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20180823T203000Z
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20180823T223000Z
UID:calendar-event-1656666228@schoology.com
URL;VALUE=URI:http://schoology.tesd.net/event/1656666228/profile
SUMMARY:9th Grade and New Family Social
DESCRIPTION:Parents and students are invited to join us for tours of the building\, to  \nmeet and greet classmates\, and enjoy water ice and soft pretzels as we  \nwelcome the class of 2022 and families new to our school district!  - Link: http://schoology.tesd.net/event/1656666228/profile
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260924T000402Z
